1
00:00:00,135 --> 00:00:01,475
See this glowing dot?

2
00:00:01,475 --> 00:00:02,910
That's the whole universe.

3
00:00:02,945 --> 00:00:03,785
To see why,

4
00:00:03,785 --> 00:00:04,605
look at this.

5
00:00:04,605 --> 00:00:07,080
This is the first real photo of a black hole,

6
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,790
released in 2019.

7
00:00:08,985 --> 00:00:09,695
It's as heavy as

8
00:00:09,695 --> 00:00:12,330
six and a half billion Suns.

9
00:00:12,330 --> 00:00:13,400
And our whole solar system

10
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,180
is this tiny circle.

11
00:00:15,715 --> 00:00:16,410
And up close,

12
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:17,895
it would look like this.

13
00:00:17,895 --> 00:00:19,775
The bright ring is hot gas,

14
00:00:19,775 --> 00:00:21,009
spinning around it.

15
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:22,659
Let's look at it from above.

16
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,235
See?

17
00:00:24,235 --> 00:00:25,967
The disk is actually flat.

18
00:00:26,085 --> 00:00:27,710
This is the back half.

19
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:29,507
And this is the front half.

20
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:30,700
As we go back down,

21
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,600
you'd expect it to hide

22
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,247
behind the black hole.

23
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:35,205
But gravity bends its light,

24
00:00:35,205 --> 00:00:36,530
up over the top...

25
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:38,247
and under the bottom.

26
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,655
In 1979,

27
00:00:39,655 --> 00:00:41,875
Jean-Pierre Luminet drew this by hand,

28
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,240
dot by dot.

29
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,995
And Interstellar's black hole

30
00:00:44,995 --> 00:00:46,710
used the same physics.

31
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,540
Now let's fly in closer.

32
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,927
Much closer.

33
00:00:50,255 --> 00:00:51,705
If you hover right here,

34
00:00:51,705 --> 00:00:52,760
the black hole fills

35
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,819
exactly half your sky.

36
00:00:54,975 --> 00:00:56,505
And see this thin line?

37
00:00:56,505 --> 00:00:57,450
It's light that goes

38
00:00:57,450 --> 00:00:59,645
all the way around the black hole...

39
00:00:59,645 --> 00:01:00,959
and comes back to you.

40
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:02,285
So in this line,

41
00:01:02,285 --> 00:01:04,569
you see the back of your own head.

42
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:05,785
Now let's go lower,

43
00:01:05,785 --> 00:01:07,805
and hover just above the edge.

44
00:01:07,805 --> 00:01:08,985
Then look up.

45
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:10,280
The whole universe shrinks

46
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:13,089
into one small dot above you.

47
00:01:13,335 --> 00:01:14,385
And down here,

48
00:01:14,385 --> 00:01:15,800
time runs slower.

49
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,145
Stay for one minute...

50
00:01:17,145 --> 00:01:19,399
and half an hour goes by out there!

51
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:21,715
And all this darkness around the dot?

52
00:01:21,715 --> 00:01:23,289
That's the black hole.
